Hi all - I've updated the proposal to further clarify it based on @sam-hickey-ibigroup and @prhod's comments. Nothing substantive changed in concept:
1. In https://github.com/google/transit/pull/221/commits/a772563cf1229d0d41cf9550e6dfca340371d809, I've explictly defined how the duplicated trip schedule and RT values are calculated as specified by @sam-hickey-ibigroup, including an example, so there is no ambiguity.
1. In https://github.com/google/transit/pull/221/commits/853eb4a21a0c7ab3d640d73b019406b6b483a882, I've added more clarity about the relationship between DUPLICATED in VehiclePositions and in TripUpdates. This uses @prhod interpretation that the `trip_id` in a VehiclePosition for a duplicated trip would be the same `trip_id` as `TripUpdate.TripProperties.trip_id`. Below is an example of of a TripUpdate that defines a new duplicated trip, and then two VehiclePositions for the original trip and the duplicated trip:

```proto
entity {
  id: "ei0"
  trip_update {
    trip: {
      trip_id: "TripId0"
      schedule_relationship: DUPLICATED
    }
    trip_properties {
      trip_id: "AddedTripId1"
      start_date: "20190821"
      start_time: "11:30:00"
    }
    stop_time_update {
	...
    }
  }
}

entity {
  id: "vehicle_position_0"
  vehicle {
    trip {
      trip_id: "TripId0"
      schedule_relationship: SCHEDULED
    }
    position {
      latitude: 28.01125
      longitude: -82.9832
    }
    timestamp: 1592515839
    vehicle {
      id: "0"
    }
  }
}

entity {
  id: "vehicle_position_1"
  vehicle {
    trip {
      trip_id: "AddedTripId1"
      schedule_relationship: DUPLICATED
    }
    position {
      latitude: 28.066446
      longitude: -82.42988
    }
    timestamp: 1592513933
    vehicle {
      id: "1"
    }
  }
}
```

In https://github.com/google/transit/pull/221/commits/fe8f4844463693a3deaf7810ec3306c64fe47c3b, I've also added further clarification that `DUPLICATED` can't be used in true frequency-based trips (exact_times=0). Re-enforcement frequency-based trips can be added in RT with the existing spec `TripUpdates` - see https://github.com/google/transit/pull/221#discussion_r443041176.

